# How to cite credgate. GitHub shows this as "Cite this repository".
# Validate after editing: nix run --inputs-from . nixpkgs#cffconvert -- --validate
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use credgate in your work, please cite it as below, and mention
  which package (R or Python) and version you used.
type: software
title: "credgate: Detect Indian Personal Data Before It Reaches Language Models"
authors:
  - given-names: Bharat
    family-names: Sikka
    email: bharat8sikka@gmail.com
  - given-names: Aishwarya
    family-names: Bais
    email: aishwarya.bais00@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  credgate detects and redacts personal data in text and data frames before
  it is sent to a large language model, with Indian identifiers built in
  (Aadhaar, PAN, GSTIN, voter ID, UPI IDs, bank and card numbers, ABHA,
  names and addresses in Latin and Indic scripts). Detection is
  deterministic: candidates are validated with checksums and scored from
  surrounding context, using a language-neutral specification shared by the
  R and Python packages.
repository-code: https://github.com/dwarpal/credgate
url: https://github.com/dwarpal/credgate
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - personal data
  - PII detection
  - redaction
  - large language models
  - India
  - DPDP Act
  - data governance
